0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the 6502 (NMOS opcodes only)
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-23). -n? does no more editing than
0000                             ;        Backspace. Ctrl-C stops every build (see the console layer); the
0000                             ;        break-off cell is BRKOFF, $047B.
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter; see b8s-z80.asm for the common ideas.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  This interpreter keeps the data stack in pages 2 and 3 (252 cells) and
0000                             ;  uses 10 bytes of zero page ($00-$09). b8s-6502-zp.asm is a smaller interpreter that
0000                             ;  keeps the stack in zero page instead (112 cells); its memory map and
0000                             ;  machine-code contract differ.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One switch, set in the EQU line below:
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks: whatever the spec calls unsafe is not caught
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build, as in the spec's "Errors and checked
0000                             ;                 builds": at startup every word cell points at 0000h (see
0000                             ;                 e_undef) and the variables and the interpreter's cells are
0000                             ;                 0. It stops with S s R r (stack over/underflow), H (heap),
0000                             ;                 O (a store outside the program's space), U (undefined
0000                             ;                 word), Q (no closing quote), W (bad character after [), X
0000                             ;                 (a reserved byte), Z (divide by zero), N (brackets) or B
0000                             ;                 (Ctrl-C), printing the spec's three-line report:
0000                             ;                   Err Z @ 3,4
0000                             ;                   Stk 2: 5 0
0000                             ;                   Rtn 0
0000                             ;                 and then goes to EXIT.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, C6502 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console codes send ANSI sequences;
0000                             ; 0 = they call CONAT, CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Registers and zero page
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    IP      zero-page pointer to the next program character (16 bits)
0000                             ;    TL/TH   the top data-stack cell (TOS) lives in zero page, not in memory
0000                             ;    X       data-stack index. The stack is two byte-planes, grows down, and
0000                             ;            holds everything under TOS: NOS is DSL,X (low) and DSH,X (high).
0000                             ;            The stack never leaves its planes because X is 8 bits.
0000                             ;    S       the hardware stack is the RETURN stack: a word call or "(" pushes
0000                             ;            the reading position (high byte first, then low) and "]" or ")"
0000                             ;            pulls it. 100 entries (200 bytes) fit with room to spare.
0000                             ;    Y, A    scratch. Y is 0 after peek/getc, and the zero-page indirect reads
0000                             ;            (IP),Y rely on that.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch: step is called with JSR, so a handler ends with a plain RTS and
0000                             ;  lands on "JMP next" in the loop. Punctuation goes through PTAB with the
0000                             ;  RTS trick (push handler-1, RTS). Handlers that use the return stack ( ( ) \
0000                             ;  ] 00bbIA== and word calls ) first pull the 2-byte JSR frame off (PLA PLA) and end
0000                             ;  with JMP next instead.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Every punctuation handler starts with the carry clear (the range sort in
0000                             ;  step leaves it so). Several of them count on that, where the comments say.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Machine-code contract (the grave): the code at TOS is entered as a
0000                             ;  subroutine, by JMP (T0) with the loop's return address on the hardware
0000                             ;  stack, so it ends with RTS (60h, which the hex loader appends). On entry
0000                             ;  TL/TH ($02/$03) hold the new TOS (the address is already consumed) and X is
0000                             ;  the data-stack index: NOS is DSL,X (low) and DSH,X (high), which is
0000                             ;  $0200,X and $0300,X.
0000                             ;  To push: DEX, store TL/TH at DSL,X/DSH,X, then set TL/TH. To drop: load
0000                             ;  TL/TH from DSL,X/DSH,X and INX. The code may change A, Y, X (it is the
0000                             ;  stack index, so it must stay consistent on return) and zero page $04-$06
0000                             ;  and $08-$09; it must keep IP ($00/$01) and the hardware stack balanced. On
0000                             ;  return TL/TH are the TOS. Zero page $0A-$0F is free for the code's own use.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                IP:       EQU   00h   ; 00-01 reading position
0000                TL:       EQU   02h   ; TOS low
0000                TH:       EQU   03h   ; TOS high
0000                T0:       EQU   04h   ; scratch
0000                T1:       EQU   05h   
0000                T2:       EQU   06h   
0000                D0:       EQU   08h   ; divisor (division, number printing)
0000                D1:       EQU   09h   
0000                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    KEYBUF:   EQU   07h   ; a key held back by the break check (0: none)
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CHECKED   
0000                PLACE:    EQU   06h   ; 06-07 (T2 and $07) the address of the
0000                             ;   character being run, for the error report:
0000                             ;   no handler of the checked build uses T2.
0000                             ;   (Machine code may change T2: that matters
0000                             ;   only if it also leaves a stack overrun,
0000                             ;   whose report then shows a wrong place.)
0000                RSV:      EQU   LET+35h   ; S as it was before this character
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; a key held back by the break check (0: none)
0000                             ; The error report runs after the program, so it may use the zero page that
0000                             ; machine code has ($0A-$0F):
0000                CL:       EQU   0Ah   ; 0A-0B the column being reported
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    0000-00FF  zero page: the variables above
0000                             ;    0100-01FF  hardware stack = return stack, S starts at FF
0000                             ;    0200       DSL, data stack, low bytes (X = FC when empty: 252 cells)
0000                             ;    0300       DSH, data stack, high bytes
0000                             ;    0400       LET  letter cells: A..Z at +00..+33, a..z at +40..+73 (a word
0000                             ;               cell is 64 bytes below its variable), heap pointer at +7C,
0000                             ;               the -n? line buffer at +80..+FF. The checked build's cells
0000                             ;               are in the gaps: RSV at +35, PEND at +38, KEYBUF (the held
0000                             ;               key; $07 in the unchecked build) at +7A; and every build's:
0000                             ;               CDOWN at +79, BRKOFF (the break-off cell) at +7B.
0000                             ;    0500       PROG the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap follows
0000                             ;    E000       the interpreter (ROM)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the page range LETPAGE..HEAPLIM-1.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (it does
0000                             ;   if the routine ends with LDA / RTS).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve X and Y.
0000                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the console codes call these four instead of sending ANSI
                                 ; sequences. All must preserve X.
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF0Ch   ; `@  cursor to row Y, column A, both from 0
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; `^  clear the screen and home the cursor
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF12h   ; `_  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF15h   ; `?  cursor off if A = 0 (the Z flag is set
                                 ;     to match), on if not
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                DSL:      EQU   0200h   ; data stack, low bytes
0000                DSH:      EQU   0300h   ; data stack, high bytes
0000                DSE:      EQU   0FCh   ; X when the data stack is empty
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   04h   
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                PROG:     EQU   0500h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                PROG1:    EQU   PROG+1   
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0E0h   ; the heap must stay below E000h (a page)
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer (the heap top)
0000                SEED:     EQU   LET+76h   ; the random seed: the cell whose address `.
0000                             ;   gives. Nothing sets it at the start but
0000                             ;   the checked build's clearing
0000                CDOWN:    EQU   LET+79h   ; the break check's countdown (see pnext)
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ; the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                PEND:     EQU   LET+38h   ; checked: the program's end, where the heap
0000                             ;   starts: it may not be released below it
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   20h   ; lowest S allowed (checked build)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ;   (each pass calls KEY once; the wait for a
0000                             ;   second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms)
0000                CWAIT:    EQU   250*MSLOOP/256   ; (that wait, in 256s)
E000                          .ORG   0E000h   
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000                             ;  Startup: find the NUL, the heap starts after it
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000   A2 FF        START:    LDX   #0FFh   
E002   9A                     TXS      ; return stack empty
E003                          IF   CHECKED   
E003                             ; The first half of the letter page is zeroed: every variable, every
E003                             ; cell of the interpreter's own (no key held back), and every word
E003                             ; cell, which then points at 0000h: calling an undefined word stops
E003                             ; with U (see e_undef).
E003   E8                     INX      
E004   8A                     TXA      ; A = 0
E005   A0 7F                  LDY   #7Fh   
E007   99 00 04     STZ:      STA   LET,Y   
E00A   88                     DEY      
E00B   10 FA                  BPL   stz   
E00D                          ENDIF      
E00D   20 C8 E2               JSR   rstip   
E010   20 BC E2     ST1:      JSR   getc   
E013   D0 FB                  BNE   st1   ; IP ends just past the NUL
E015                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              STA   KEYBUF   ; (A = 0) no key held, the break key on
                              STA   BRKOFF   
E015                          ENDIF      
E015   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E017   8D 7C 04               STA   HEAP   
E01A                          IF   CHECKED   
E01A   8D 38 04               STA   PEND   
E01D                          ENDIF      
E01D   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E01F   8D 7D 04               STA   HEAP+1   
E022                          IF   CHECKED   
E022   8D 39 04               STA   PEND+1   
E025                          ENDIF      
E025   20 C8 E2               JSR   rstip   
E028   A2 FC                  LDX   #DSE   
E02A                             ; =============================================================================
E02A                             ;  The inner loop
E02A                             ; =============================================================================
E02A                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
E02A                             ;  The break key. A running program reads the keyboard only through getk
E02A                             ;  (for "?") and pnext (the break check), which between them give the break
E02A                             ;  key its rules:
E02A                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program: silently to EXIT in the unchecked
E02A                             ;      build, with the report (B) in the checked one;
E02A                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
E02A                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
E02A                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
E02A                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
E02A                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
E02A                             ;  KEY is the host's: a waiting key in A, or A = 0 with the zero flag set.
E02A                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
E02A                             ; pnext: the break check, then (falling through) next. A word call, a true
E02A                             ; "(" and a true ")" end here, but the keyboard is looked at only once in 256
E02A                             ; of them: CDOWN counts them down. A key found is held; a Ctrl-C goes on to ctlc. (Startup
E02A                             ; falls in here too, which does no harm.)
E02A   CE 79 04     PNEXT:    DEC   CDOWN   
E02D   D0 0B                  BNE   next   
E02F   20 06 FF               JSR   KEY   
E032   F0 06                  BEQ   next   ; no key
E034   8D 7A 04               STA   KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
E037   20 CC E0               JSR   chk3   ; (Ctrl-C: back only if the break key is off)
E03A                NEXT:        
E03A                          IF   CHECKED   
E03A                             ; Both stacks are checked once per character, after it has run. The
E03A                             ; return stack has overrun when S is below RSLIM: an overflow leaves
E03A                             ; it at 1Eh or 1Fh, an underflow wraps it to 01h (no handler pulls
E03A                             ; more than one entry). The data stack has when X is above DSE: an
E03A                             ; underflow moves X up to FDh or FEh (no handler moves X by more
E03A                             ; than 2), and an overflow wraps it from 00h to FFh.
E03A                             ; S is kept in RSV, for the report's Rtn line (an error found inside
E03A                             ; a handler has its own calls on the hardware stack), and the place
E03A                             ; of the character about to run in PLACE.
E03A   8A                     TXA      ; TSX trashes X: keep it in A
E03B   BA                     TSX      
E03C   8E 35 04               STX   RSV   
E03F   E0 20                  CPX   #RSLIM   
E041   AA                     TAX      ; TAX leaves the carry alone
E042   90 12                  BCC   e_rstack   
E044   E0 FD                  CPX   #DSE+1   
E046   B0 20                  BCS   e_stack   
E048   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E04A   85 06                  STA   PLACE   
E04C   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E04E   85 07                  STA   PLACE+1   
E050                          ENDIF      
E050   20 12 E1               JSR   step   
E053   4C 3A E0               JMP   next   
E056                          IF   CHECKED   
E056                             ; S/R are overflows, s/r underflows. After an underflow that stack counts as
E056                             ; empty.
E056   AD 35 04     E_RSTACK:   LDA   RSV   
E059   C9 10                  CMP   #10h   
E05B   A9 52                  LDA   #"R"   
E05D   B0 13                  BCS   ejmp   ; S is 1Eh-1Fh: an overflow
E05F   A9 FF                  LDA   #0FFh   
E061   8D 35 04               STA   RSV   ; S wrapped to 01h: Rtn 0
E064   A9 72                  LDA   #"r"   
E066   D0 0A                  BNE   ejmp   ; always
E068   E0 FF        E_STACK:   CPX   #0FFh   
E06A   A9 53                  LDA   #"S"   
E06C   B0 04                  BCS   ejmp   ; X wrapped from 00h to FFh: an overflow
E06E   A2 FC                  LDX   #DSE   ; an underflow: Stk 0
E070   A9 73                  LDA   #"s"   
E072   4C A7 E6     EJMP:     JMP   error   
E075                          ENDIF      
E075                             ; The handlers that work on the return stack sit here, where short branches
E075                             ; reach next and pnext.
E075                             ; "{" TOS to the return stack, "}" return stack to TOS
E075   68           H_TOR:    PLA      
E076   68                     PLA      
E077   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E079   48                     PHA      
E07A   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E07C   48                     PHA      
E07D   20 F1 E2               JSR   drop   
E080   D0 B8                  BNE   next   ; always
E082   68           H_FROMR:   PLA      
E083   68                     PLA      
E084   20 76 E1               JSR   push   
E087   68                     PLA      
E088   85 02                  STA   TL   
E08A   68                     PLA      
E08B   85 03                  STA   TH   
E08D   90 AB                  BCC   next   ; always: the carry is clear on the way in
E08F                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
E08F                             ; drops it and carries on. It shares "]"s code: with the carry clear, as
E08F                             ; it is here, the address popped is pushed back.
E08F   20 D1 E2     H_CLOSE:   JSR   flag   
E092   F0 20                  BEQ   rdrop   
E094   24                     DB   24h   ; (BIT zp: steps over the SEC)
E095                             ; "]" returns: pull an address and jump to it.
E095   38           H_RET:    SEC      
E096   68                     PLA      
E097   68                     PLA      ; drop the step frame
E098   68                     PLA      
E099   85 00                  STA   IP   
E09B   68                     PLA      
E09C   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E09E   B0 9A                  BCS   next   
E0A0   48                     PHA      ; ")": keep the block start
E0A1   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E0A3   48                     PHA      
E0A4   90 84                  BCC   pnext   ; always: a loop-back, with the break check
E0A6                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
E0A6                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns.
E0A6   20 D1 E2     H_BREAK:   JSR   flag   
E0A9   F0 25                  BEQ   gk9   ; (an RTS)
E0AB                          IF   CHECKED   
E0AB   A9 00                  LDA   #0   ; \ takes either closer
E0AD                          ENDIF      
E0AD   20 D1 E1               JSR   skip   
E0B0   C9 29                  CMP   #")"   
E0B2   D0 E1                  BNE   h_ret   
E0B4   68           RDROP:    PLA      
E0B5   68                     PLA      
E0B6   68                     PLA      
E0B7   68                     PLA      ; (the block start's high byte: never 0)
E0B8   D0 80                  BNE   next   ; always
E0BA                             ; getk: a key for "?" in A (zero flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag
E0BA                             ; set when there is none. Keeps X and Y. The held key goes first, and is
E0BA                             ; taken out of KEYBUF.
E0BA   AD 7A 04     GETK:     LDA   KEYBUF   
E0BD   F0 08                  BEQ   gk1   
E0BF   48                     PHA      
E0C0   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E0C2   8D 7A 04               STA   KEYBUF   
E0C5   68                     PLA      
E0C6   60                     RTS      
E0C7   20 06 FF     GK1:      JSR   KEY   
E0CA   F0 04                  BEQ   gk9   
E0CC                             ; chk3: a key in A (not 0). A Ctrl-C goes on to ctlc, which gives the 03h
E0CC                             ; back if it comes back at all.
E0CC   C9 03        CHK3:     CMP   #3   
E0CE   F0 01                  BEQ   ctlc   
E0D0   60           GK9:      RTS      
E0D1                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
E0D1                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms (about 250 times MSLOOP
E0D1                             ; looks: D0 counts the 256s, D1 runs on from whatever it holds) for one more
E0D1                             ; key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest
E0D1                             ; wins). Returns A = 03h with the zero flag clear. Keeps X and Y.
E0D1   AD 7B 04     CTLC:     LDA   BRKOFF   
E0D4   F0 1D                  BEQ   cbreak   
E0D6   A9 28                  LDA   #CWAIT+1   
E0D8   85 08                  STA   D0   
E0DA   20 06 FF     CT2:      JSR   KEY   
E0DD   D0 0A                  BNE   ct3   
E0DF   C6 09                  DEC   D1   
E0E1   D0 F7                  BNE   ct2   
E0E3   C6 08                  DEC   D0   
E0E5   D0 F3                  BNE   ct2   
E0E7   F0 07                  BEQ   ct9   ; always: none came
E0E9   C9 03        CT3:      CMP   #3   
E0EB   F0 06                  BEQ   cbreak   
E0ED   8D 7A 04               STA   KEYBUF   
E0F0   A9 03        CT9:      LDA   #3   
E0F2   60                     RTS      
E0F3                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    CBREAK:   EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
E0F3                          ENDIF      
E0F3                          IF   CHECKED   
E0F3                CBREAK:   EQU   e_break   ; the checked build reports B
E0F3                          ENDIF      
E0F3                          IF   CHECKED   
E0F3   A9 42        E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C (the stacks as they stand)
E0F5   2C                     DB   2Ch   
E0F6   A9 58        E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte, 80h-FFh
E0F8   4C A7 E6     EJMP3:    JMP   error   
E0FB                          ENDIF      
E0FB                          IF   CHECKED   
E0FB                             ; e_undef: the word cells of undefined words hold 0000h. A call there reads
E0FB                             ; the byte at 0000h, which is IP's own low byte: 00h while IP is 0000h, so
E0FB                             ; the call reads a NUL with IP in page zero, where no program can be. The
E0FB                             ; call is undone first: the step frame and the return address come off the
E0FB                             ; hardware stack, and the place is the call letter (the return address - 1).
E0FB   68           E_UNDEF:   PLA      
E0FC   68                     PLA      ; the step frame
E0FD   68                     PLA      
E0FE   38                     SEC      
E0FF   E9 01                  SBC   #1   
E101   85 06                  STA   PLACE   
E103   68                     PLA      
E104   E9 00                  SBC   #0   
E106   85 07                  STA   PLACE+1   
E108   EE 35 04               INC   RSV   
E10B   EE 35 04               INC   RSV   ; Rtn does not count the call
E10E   A9 55                  LDA   #"U"   
E110   D0 E6                  BNE   ejmp3   ; always
E112                          ENDIF      
E112                             ; step: read one character and sort it by range.
E112                             ;    00h          end of program
E112                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored
E112                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
E112                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
E112                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
E112                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
E112                             ; Every way out of the sort has the carry clear, except "ignored". A checked
E112                             ; build stops on 80h-FFh (X) and still ignores DEL.
E112   20 BC E2     STEP:     JSR   getc   ; flags follow A
E115   F0 38                  BEQ   endprog   
E117   38                     SEC      
E118   E9 21                  SBC   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
E11A   90 32                  BCC   ign   ; 01h-20h
E11C   C9 0F                  CMP   #0Fh   
E11E   90 24                  BCC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: index 0-14
E120   E9 0F                  SBC   #0Fh   ; (carry set) A = c - 30h
E122   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E124   90 35                  BCC   digit   
E126   C9 11                  CMP   #11h   
E128   90 18                  BCC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
E12A   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (carry set) A = c - 41h
E12C   C9 1A                  CMP   #1Ah   
E12E   90 26                  BCC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah
E130   C9 20                  CMP   #20h   
E132   90 0C                  BCC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
E134   C9 3A                  CMP   #3Ah   
E136   90 2B                  BCC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h
E138   C9 3E                  CMP   #3Eh   
E13A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BCS   ign   ; 7Fh-FFh
E13A                          ENDIF      
E13A                          IF   CHECKED   
E13A   F0 12                  BEQ   ign   ; 7Fh
E13C   B0 B8                  BCS   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
E13E                          ENDIF      
E13E                             ; The three adjustments below chain. Each ADC adds the carry the one
E13E                             ; before it left, which the constants allow for.
E13E   E9 1A                  SBC   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: (carry clear: -1Bh) index 28-31
E140   69 F6        P5B:      ADC   #0F6h   ; 5Bh-60h: -10 (-9 when chained), index 22-27
E142   69 05        P3A:      ADC   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: +5 (+6 when chained), index 15-21
E144   0A           PUNCT:    ASL      ; (the index is small: the carry stays clear)
E145   A8                     TAY      
E146   B9 30 E2               LDA   PTAB+1,Y   
E149   48                     PHA      
E14A   B9 2F E2               LDA   PTAB,Y   
E14D   48                     PHA      
E14E   60           IGN:      RTS      ; RTS trick: goes to the handler. Reached
E14F                             ; directly, it just ends an ignored character.
E14F                ENDPROG:      
E14F                          IF   CHECKED   
E14F   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   ; IP in page zero: an undefined word
E151   F0 A8                  BEQ   e_undef   
E153                          ENDIF      
E153   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   
E156                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
E156                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
E156   0A           UPPER:    ASL      
E157   A8                     TAY      
E158   38                     SEC      
E159   B0 2C                  BCS   pushn   ; always
E15B                             ; Digits: the first one is in A; read the rest of the number.
E15B   A0 00        DIGIT:    LDY   #0   
E15D   20 6C E1               JSR   pushay   
E160   4C 96 E2               JMP   rdnum   
E163                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
E163   0A           LOWER:    ASL      
E164   A0 04                  LDY   #>LET   
E166   D0 04                  BNE   pushay   ; always
E168   A5 00        PUSHIP:   LDA   IP   ; push the reading position
E16A   A4 01                  LDY   IP+1   
E16C                             ; pushay: push a cell: A = its low byte, Y = its high byte
E16C   48           PUSHAY:   PHA      
E16D   20 76 E1               JSR   push   
E170   68                     PLA      
E171   85 02                  STA   TL   
E173   84 03                  STY   TH   
E175   60                     RTS      
E176   CA           PUSH:     DEX      ; ":" and every push (keeps Y)
E177   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E179   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E17C   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E17E   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E181   60                     RTS      
E182                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
E182                             ; the matching ")".
E182   20 D1 E2     H_OPEN:   JSR   flag   ; (keeps the carry clear)
E185                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   skip   
E185                          ENDIF      
E185                          IF   CHECKED   
E185   F0 25                  BEQ   skpar   
E187                          ENDIF      
E187                             ; pushn: take the step frame off, push the reading position on the return
E187                             ; stack, and go on. With the carry set (a word call) the reading position
E187                             ; then becomes the address in the letter cell at LET,Y.
E187   68           PUSHN:    PLA      
E188   68                     PLA      ; drop the step frame
E189   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E18B   48                     PHA      
E18C   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E18E   48                     PHA      
E18F   90 0A                  BCC   nxt   
E191   B9 00 04               LDA   LET,Y   
E194   85 00                  STA   IP   
E196   B9 01 04               LDA   LET+1,Y   
E199   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E19B   4C 2A E0     NXT:      JMP   pnext   
E19E                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
E19E                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
E19E                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
E19E                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
E19E                             ; checked build stops on it.)
E19E                          IF   CHECKED   
E19E   C0 DF        DEF1:     CPY   #" "-"A"+256   
E1A0   F0 2A                  BEQ   def2   
E1A2                             ; W: anything but a letter or a space after [. The place is that character,
E1A2                             ; one past the [.
E1A2   E6 06                  INC   PLACE   
E1A4   D0 02                  BNE   eb1   
E1A6   E6 07                  INC   PLACE+1   
E1A8   A9 57        EB1:      LDA   #"W"   
E1AA   D0 62                  BNE   ejmp2   ; always
E1AC                             ; A false ( skips: the wrong closer for it is ].
E1AC   A9 5D        SKPAR:    LDA   #"]"   
E1AE   D0 21                  BNE   skip   ; always
E1B0                          ENDIF      
E1B0   20 BC E2     H_DEF:    JSR   getc   
E1B3   38                     SEC      
E1B4   E9 41                  SBC   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
E1B6   A8                     TAY      ;   lands 64 bytes up
E1B7   29 DF                  AND   #0DFh   ; fold case: 0-25 only for a letter
E1B9   C9 1A                  CMP   #26   
E1BB                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BCS   def2   ; not a letter
E1BB                          ENDIF      
E1BB                          IF   CHECKED   
E1BB   B0 E1                  BCS   def1   
E1BD                          ENDIF      
E1BD   98                     TYA      
E1BE   0A                     ASL      
E1BF   A8                     TAY      ; Y -> the cell
E1C0   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E1C2   99 00 04               STA   LET,Y   
E1C5   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E1C7   99 01 04               STA   LET+1,Y   
E1CA   D0 03                  BNE   skdef   ; always: no program is in page zero
E1CC   20 68 E1     DEF2:     JSR   puship   ; an anonymous block: push its address
E1CF                SKDEF:       
E1CF                          IF   CHECKED   
E1CF   A9 29                  LDA   #")"   ; the wrong closer for [
E1D1                          ENDIF      
E1D1                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return it in A.
E1D1                             ; Brackets of both kinds count together; strings are stepped over whole. A
E1D1                             ; NUL first ends the program.
E1D1                             ; In the checked build A holds, on the way in, the wrong closer for the
E1D1                             ; opener that started the skip, kept in T0: ] for (, ) for [, and 0 for \,
E1D1                             ; which takes either. Meeting the wrong closer at this level, or the end
E1D1                             ; (a NUL, or a string that runs into it), stops with N, except for \,
E1D1                             ; which then ends the program as before.
E1D1                SKIP:        
E1D1                          IF   CHECKED   
E1D1   85 04                  STA   T0   
E1D3                          ENDIF      
E1D3   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E1D5   85 09                  STA   D1   ; depth
E1D7   20 BC E2     SK1:      JSR   getc   
E1DA                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   endprog   
E1DA                          ENDIF      
E1DA                          IF   CHECKED   
E1DA   F0 26                  BEQ   sknul   
E1DC                          ENDIF      
E1DC   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E1DE   D0 05                  BNE   sk2   
E1E0   20 1A E2               JSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h (11h when checked), which
E1E3                             ;   matches nothing below
E1E3                          IF   CHECKED   
E1E3   F0 1D                  BEQ   sknul   ; the string ran into the end
E1E5                          ENDIF      
E1E5   C9 28        SK2:      CMP   #"("   
E1E7   F0 15                  BEQ   sk3   
E1E9   C9 5B                  CMP   #"["   
E1EB   F0 11                  BEQ   sk3   
E1ED   C9 29                  CMP   #")"   
E1EF   F0 04                  BEQ   sk4   
E1F1   C9 5D                  CMP   #"]"   
E1F3   D0 E2                  BNE   sk1   
E1F5   C6 09        SK4:      DEC   D1   
E1F7   10 DE                  BPL   sk1   
E1F9                          IF   CHECKED   
E1F9   C5 04                  CMP   T0   
E1FB   F0 0C                  BEQ   e_nest   ; the wrong kind
E1FD                          ENDIF      
E1FD   60                     RTS      ; the closer at this level
E1FE   E6 09        SK3:      INC   D1   
E200   D0 D5                  BNE   sk1   
E202                          IF   CHECKED   
E202   A5 04        SKNUL:    LDA   T0   
E204   D0 03                  BNE   e_nest   ; ( and [ stop with N
E206   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   ; \ ends the program
E209   A9 4E        E_NEST:   LDA   #"N"   ; a skip from ( or [ found the wrong closer
E20B   2C                     DB   2Ch   ;   or the end: the place is the opener
E20C   A9 51        E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; a string from 22h runs into the end
E20E   4C A7 E6     EJMP2:    JMP   error   
E211                          ENDIF      
E211                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
E211   20 68 E1     H_STR:    JSR   puship   
E214                          IF   CHECKED   
E214   20 1A E2               JSR   skipstr   
E217   F0 F3                  BEQ   e_quote   ; it ran into the end: the place is the 22h
E219   60                     RTS      
E21A                          ENDIF      
E21A                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
E21A                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it.
E21A                             ; Unchecked, it returns with Z set and A = 22h, and it does not look for the
E21A                             ; end. Checked, it returns with Z clear and A = 11h, or with Z set if the
E21A                             ; text ended first (a NUL, also one just after "/").
E21A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
                              CMP   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMP   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      
                    SS0:      JSR   incip   
                              BNE   skipstr   ; A is "/" here
E21A                          ENDIF      
E21A                          IF   CHECKED   
E21A   20 BC E2     SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
E21D   F0 09                  BEQ   ss9   ; the end
E21F   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E221   D0 06                  BNE   ss1   
E223   20 BC E2               JSR   getc   ; the escaped character
E226   D0 F2                  BNE   skipstr   
E228   60           SS9:      RTS      ; the end, just after "/"
E229   C9 22        SS1:      CMP   #22h   
E22B   D0 ED                  BNE   skipstr   
E22D   4A                     LSR      ; A = 11h, Z clear
E22E   60                     RTS      
E22F                          ENDIF      
E22F                             ; =============================================================================
E22F                             ;  Dispatch table: one handler per punctuation character, in code order.
E22F                             ;  Entries are handler-1 for the RTS trick.
E22F                             ; =============================================================================
E22F   D9 E2        PTAB:     DW   h_store-1   ; !
E231   10 E2                  DW   h_str-1   ; "
E233   C4 E4                  DW   h_num-1   ; #
E235   95 E4                  DW   h_print-1   ; $
E237   AB E3                  DW   h_swap-1   ; %
E239   FC E2                  DW   h_and-1   ; &
E23B   BC E4                  DW   h_emit-1   ; '
E23D   81 E1                  DW   h_open-1   ; (
E23F   8E E0                  DW   h_close-1   ; )
E241   83 E3                  DW   h_mul-1   ; *
E243   2E E3                  DW   h_add-1   ; +
E245   FF E4                  DW   h_cfetch-1   ; ,
E247   26 E3                  DW   h_sub-1   ; -
E249   E3 E2                  DW   h_cstore-1   ; .
E24B   C0 E3                  DW   h_div-1   ; /
E24D   75 E1                  DW   push-1   ; :
E24F   F0 E2                  DW   drop-1   ; ;
E251   5D E3                  DW   h_lt-1   ; <
E253   73 E3                  DW   h_eq-1   ; =
E255   5A E3                  DW   h_gt-1   ; >
E257   08 E5                  DW   h_key-1   ; ?
E259   F3 E4                  DW   h_fetch-1   ; @
E25B   AF E1                  DW   h_def-1   ; [
E25D   A5 E0                  DW   h_break-1   ; \
E25F   94 E0                  DW   h_ret-1   ; ]
E261   18 E3                  DW   h_xor-1   ; ^
E263   F3 E3                  DW   h_alloc-1   ; _
E265   71 E5                  DW   h_grave-1   ; `
E267   74 E0                  DW   h_tor-1   ; {
E269   0A E3                  DW   h_or-1   ; |
E26B   81 E0                  DW   h_fromr-1   ; }
E26D   46 E3                  DW   h_not-1   ; ~
E26F                             ; rdnum: TOS = TOS*10 + digit for each digit at IP. Wraps at 16 bits. The
E26F                             ; test is at the bottom so the loop closes with a branch. Returns with the
E26F                             ; carry set.
E26F   20 BF E2     RD1:      JSR   incip   ; (keeps A = the digit)
E272   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E274   26 03                  ROL   TH   ; x2
E276   18                     CLC      
E277   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E279   85 04                  STA   T0   
E27B   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E27D   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E27F   85 05                  STA   T1   ; T = x2 + digit
E281   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E283   26 03                  ROL   TH   
E285   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E287   26 03                  ROL   TH   ; x8
E289   18                     CLC      
E28A   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E28C   65 04                  ADC   T0   
E28E   85 02                  STA   TL   
E290   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E292   65 05                  ADC   T1   
E294   85 03                  STA   TH   ; x8 + x2 + digit
E296   20 9C E2     RDNUM:    JSR   isdig   
E299   90 D4                  BCC   rd1   
E29B   60                     RTS      
E29C                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is clear if it is a
E29C                             ; digit. Y = 0.
E29C   20 B7 E2     ISDIG:    JSR   peek   
E29F   38                     SEC      
E2A0   E9 30                  SBC   #"0"   
E2A2   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E2A4   60                     RTS      
E2A5                             ; =============================================================================
E2A5                             ;  Reading the program
E2A5                             ;    peek: A = the character at IP, IP unchanged, Y = 0
E2A5                             ;    getc: the same, then IP moves on; flags follow A
E2A5                             ;    incip: IP moves on; keeps A, the carry and Y
E2A5                             ; =============================================================================
E2A5                             ; rdhex: if IP is at a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), return its value in A with
E2A5                             ; the carry clear and IP moved on; otherwise the carry is set and IP stays.
E2A5                             ; Y = 0.
E2A5   20 9C E2     RDHEX:    JSR   isdig   
E2A8   90 0A                  BCC   rh1   
E2AA   29 DF                  AND   #0DFh   
E2AC   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (the carry is set)
E2AE   C9 06                  CMP   #6   
E2B0   B0 04                  BCS   rh9   
E2B2   69 0A                  ADC   #10   
E2B4   90 09        RH1:      BCC   incip   ; always: the carry is clear
E2B6   60           RH9:      RTS      
E2B7   A0 00        PEEK:     LDY   #0   
E2B9   B1 00                  LDA   (IP),Y   
E2BB   60                     RTS      
E2BC   20 B7 E2     GETC:     JSR   peek   
E2BF   E6 00        INCIP:    INC   IP   
E2C1   D0 02                  BNE   ic1   
E2C3   E6 01                  INC   IP+1   
E2C5   09 00        IC1:      ORA   #0   
E2C7   60                     RTS      
E2C8                             ; rstip: point IP at the start of the program
E2C8   A9 00        RSTIP:    LDA   #<PROG   
E2CA   85 00                  STA   IP   
E2CC   A9 05                  LDA   #>PROG   
E2CE   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E2D0   60                     RTS      
E2D1                             ; =============================================================================
E2D1                             ;  Stack
E2D1                             ; =============================================================================
E2D1                             ; flag: pops TOS and returns with Z set if it was 0. Keeps the carry.
E2D1   A5 02        FLAG:     LDA   TL   
E2D3   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E2D5   20 F1 E2               JSR   drop   
E2D8   A8                     TAY      ; (drop's INX changed the flags)
E2D9   60                     RTS      
E2DA                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." plus the high byte. Both end in drop.
E2DA                H_STORE:      
E2DA                          IF   CHECKED   
E2DA   20 34 E4               JSR   chk2   ; both bytes must be in the program's space
E2DD                          ENDIF      
E2DD   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E2E0   A0 01                  LDY   #1   
E2E2   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E2E4                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
E2E4                          IF   CHECKED   
E2E4   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E2E6   20 41 E4               JSR   chkst   
E2E9                          ENDIF      
E2E9   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E2EC   A0 00                  LDY   #0   
E2EE   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E2F0   E8                     INX      ; falls into drop
E2F1                             ; drop: ";" and every drop. It works through Y, so A and the carry are kept;
E2F1                             ; it returns with Z clear.
E2F1   BC 00 02     DROP:     LDY   DSL,X   
E2F4   84 02                  STY   TL   
E2F6   BC 00 03               LDY   DSH,X   
E2F9   84 03                  STY   TH   
E2FB   E8                     INX      
E2FC   60                     RTS      
E2FD                             ; =============================================================================
E2FD                             ;  Arithmetic and logic. Effects are ( NOS TOS -- result ).
E2FD                             ; =============================================================================
E2FD                             ; The logic operators leave the carry as they found it, clear, so they can
E2FD                             ; branch to fin.
E2FD   BD 00 02     H_AND:    LDA   DSL,X   
E300   25 02                  AND   TL   
E302   85 02                  STA   TL   
E304   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E307   25 03                  AND   TH   
E309   90 31                  BCC   fin   ; always
E30B   BD 00 02     H_OR:     LDA   DSL,X   
E30E   05 02                  ORA   TL   
E310   85 02                  STA   TL   
E312   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E315   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E317   90 23                  BCC   fin   ; always
E319   BD 00 02     H_XOR:    LDA   DSL,X   
E31C   45 02                  EOR   TL   
E31E   85 02                  STA   TL   
E320   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E323   45 03                  EOR   TH   
E325   90 15                  BCC   fin   ; always
E327                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
E327   20 9C E2     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
E32A   90 14                  BCC   negnum   
E32C   20 4D E3     SUB1:     JSR   neg   ; a - b = a + (-b)
E32F   18           H_ADD:    CLC      
E330   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E333   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E335   85 02                  STA   TL   
E337   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E33A   65 03                  ADC   TH   ; falls into fin
E33C                             ; fin: finish a two-operand op: A = the high byte of the result
E33C   85 03        FIN:      STA   TH   
E33E   E8                     INX      
E33F   60                     RTS      
E340   A9 00        NEGNUM:   LDA   #0   ; a number from 0 (the digit routine's start)
E342   20 5B E1               JSR   digit   ; (comes back with the carry set)
E345   B0 06                  BCS   neg   ; always: the number, negated
E347                             ; "~": -x - 1, which is neg with the carry clear, as it is here
E347   90 05        H_NOT:    BCC   neg1   ; always
E349                             ; absv: TOS = |TOS|.  negm: TOS = -TOS if the N flag is set.
E349   A5 03        ABSV:     LDA   TH   
E34B   10 0D        NEGM:     BPL   ab9   
E34D                             ; neg: TOS = -TOS
E34D   38           NEG:      SEC      
E34E   A9 00        NEG1:     LDA   #0   
E350   E5 02                  SBC   TL   
E352   85 02                  STA   TL   
E354   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E356   E5 03                  SBC   TH   
E358   85 03                  STA   TH   
E35A   60           AB9:      RTS      
E35B                             ; Signed compares: a - b sets N and V; N xor V is "a < b". The carry ends up
E35B                             ; clear for true, and bool turns it into -1 (true) or 0 (both pop NOS first).
E35B   20 AC E3     H_GT:     JSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
E35E   20 64 E3     H_LT:     JSR   scmp   
E361   E8                     INX      ; (keeps the carry; never leaves X at 0)
E362   D0 17                  BNE   bool   ; always
E364                             ; scmp: the carry clear if NOS < TOS (signed). `< and `> use it too.
E364   BD 00 02     SCMP:     LDA   DSL,X   
E367   C5 02                  CMP   TL   
E369   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E36C   E5 03                  SBC   TH   
E36E   70 02                  BVS   lt1   
E370   49 80                  EOR   #80h   
E372   0A           LT1:      ASL      
E373   60                     RTS      
E374   20 2C E3     H_EQ:     JSR   sub1   ; a - b: zero if equal; A = its high byte
E377   05 02                  ORA   TL   
E379   C9 01                  CMP   #1   ; carry clear if A = 0
E37B   A9 00        BOOL:     LDA   #0   
E37D   69 FF                  ADC   #0FFh   ; carry clear: FF, set: 00
E37F   85 02                  STA   TL   
E381   85 03                  STA   TH   
E383   60                     RTS      
E384                             ; "*": the classic shift-right multiply. The multiplier leaves TH:TL from the
E384                             ; bottom while the product comes in at the top, through A:T0 above it; after
E384                             ; 16 rounds TH:TL hold the low 16 bits, which are all that is kept.
E384   A0 10        H_MUL:    LDY   #16   
E386   84 05                  STY   T1   ; the round count
E388   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E38A   85 04                  STA   T0   ; A:T0 = the upper half
E38C   46 03                  LSR   TH   
E38E   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; the first multiplier bit
E390   90 0D        ML1:      BCC   ml2   
E392   A8                     TAY      
E393   18                     CLC      
E394   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E396   7D 00 02               ADC   DSL,X   
E399   85 04                  STA   T0   
E39B   98                     TYA      
E39C   7D 00 03               ADC   DSH,X   ; upper half += the multiplicand
E39F   6A           ML2:      ROR      
E3A0   66 04                  ROR   T0   
E3A2   66 03                  ROR   TH   
E3A4   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; everything one place right; next bit out
E3A6   C6 05                  DEC   T1   
E3A8   D0 E6                  BNE   ml1   
E3AA   E8                     INX      ; drop the multiplicand
E3AB   60                     RTS      
E3AC   BC 00 02     H_SWAP:   LDY   DSL,X   ; "%"
E3AF   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E3B1   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E3B4   84 02                  STY   TL   
E3B6   BC 00 03               LDY   DSH,X   
E3B9   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E3BB   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E3BE   84 03                  STY   TH   
E3C0   60                     RTS      
E3C1                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
E3C1                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
E3C1                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
E3C1                             ; it stops with Z.
E3C1                H_DIV:       
E3C1                          IF   CHECKED   
E3C1   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E3C3   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E3C5   F0 62                  BEQ   e_zero   
E3C7                          ENDIF      
E3C7   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E3CA   48                     PHA      ; a's sign: for r
E3CB   45 03                  EOR   TH   
E3CD   48                     PHA      ; a xor b: for q
E3CE   20 49 E3               JSR   absv   
E3D1   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E3D3   85 08                  STA   D0   
E3D5   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E3D7   85 09                  STA   D1   ; D = |b|
E3D9   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E3DC   85 02                  STA   TL   
E3DE   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E3E1   85 03                  STA   TH   
E3E3   20 49 E3               JSR   absv   ; TOS = |a|
E3E6   20 4A E4               JSR   udiv   ; TOS = q, NOS = r
E3E9   68                     PLA      
E3EA   20 4B E3               JSR   negm   ; q's sign
E3ED   20 AC E3               JSR   h_swap   ; r on top
E3F0   68                     PLA      
E3F1   4C 4B E3               JMP   negm   ; r's sign
E3F4                             ; =============================================================================
E3F4                             ;  Storage
E3F4                             ; =============================================================================
E3F4                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap top moves by n, which is signed: a negative
E3F4                             ; count releases. TOS becomes the old top. (The carry is clear on the way in.)
E3F4                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_ALLOC:   LDA   HEAP   
                              TAY      
                              ADC   TL   
                              STA   HEAP   
                              STY   TL   
                              LDA   HEAP+1   
                              TAY      
                              ADC   TH   
                              STA   HEAP+1   
                              STY   TH   
                              RTS      
E3F4                          ENDIF      
E3F4                             ; The checked build works the new top out first, in T0 and Y, and stops with
E3F4                             ; H, the count still on the stack, if it is at or past the limit, below the
E3F4                             ; program's end, or if the 16-bit add wrapped. A wrap is the V flag of the
E3F4                             ; high bytes" add with the old top"s sign bit flipped: that makes the old top
E3F4                             ; a signed number from -8000h, so the add overflows exactly when the true
E3F4                             ; sum leaves 0000h-FFFFh.
E3F4                          IF   CHECKED   
E3F4   AD 7C 04     H_ALLOC:   LDA   HEAP   
E3F7   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E3F9   85 04                  STA   T0   
E3FB   AD 7D 04               LDA   HEAP+1   
E3FE   49 80                  EOR   #80h   
E400   65 03                  ADC   TH   
E402   70 28                  BVS   e_heap   ; wrapped
E404   49 80                  EOR   #80h   ; the new top's high byte
E406   C9 E0                  CMP   #HEAPLIM   
E408   B0 22                  BCS   e_heap   ; at or past the limit
E40A   A8                     TAY      
E40B   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E40D   CD 38 04               CMP   PEND   
E410   98                     TYA      
E411   ED 39 04               SBC   PEND+1   
E414   90 16                  BCC   e_heap   ; below the program's end
E416   AD 7C 04               LDA   HEAP   
E419   85 02                  STA   TL   
E41B   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E41D   8D 7C 04               STA   HEAP   
E420   AD 7D 04               LDA   HEAP+1   
E423   85 03                  STA   TH   
E425   8C 7D 04               STY   HEAP+1   
E428   60                     RTS      
E429                             ; Errors found by handlers. The stacks are as they were before the handler.
E429   A9 5A        E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; divide by zero
E42B   2C                     DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
E42C   A9 48        E_HEAP:   LDA   #"H"   ; heap past the limit or below the program
E42E   2C                     DB   2Ch   
E42F   A9 4F        E_STORE:   LDA   #"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
E431   4C A7 E6               JMP   error   
E434                             ; chk2: stop unless the cell at TOS, both its bytes, is in the program's own
E434                             ; space: the page of addr+1 (CMP sets the carry if addr ends in FFh), then of
E434                             ; addr. "!" and the grave's `+ and `- use it. Keeps Y.
E434   A5 02        CHK2:     LDA   TL   
E436   C9 FF                  CMP   #0FFh   
E438   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E43A   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E43C   20 41 E4               JSR   chkst   
E43F   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E441                             ; chkst: stop unless the page in A is in the program's own space, from the
E441                             ; letter page up to the heap limit. Keeps Y.
E441   C9 04        CHKST:    CMP   #LETPAGE   
E443   90 EA                  BCC   e_store   
E445   C9 E0                  CMP   #HEAPLIM   
E447   B0 E6                  BCS   e_store   
E449   60                     RTS      
E44A                          ENDIF      
E44A                             ; udiv: unsigned TOS / D (D <= 8000h). TOS becomes the quotient and the NOS
E44A                             ; cell the remainder (whatever was there is lost).
E44A                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
E44A   A9 00        UDIV:     LDA   #0   
E44C   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E44F   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E452   A5 08                  LDA   D0   
E454   49 02                  EOR   #2   
E456   05 09                  ORA   D1   
E458   D0 08                  BNE   ud0   
E45A   46 03                  LSR   TH   
E45C   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; the quotient
E45E   3E 00 02               ROL   DSL,X   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
E461   60                     RTS      
E462   A0 10        UD0:      LDY   #16   
E464   06 02        UD1:      ASL   TL   
E466   26 03                  ROL   TH   
E468   3E 00 02               ROL   DSL,X   
E46B   3E 00 03               ROL   DSH,X   
E46E   38                     SEC      
E46F   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E472   E5 08                  SBC   D0   
E474   85 04                  STA   T0   
E476   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E479   E5 09                  SBC   D1   
E47B   90 0A                  BCC   ud2   
E47D   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E480   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E482   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E485   E6 02                  INC   TL   ; the quotient bit (TL's bit 0 is free)
E487   88           UD2:      DEY      
E488   D0 DA                  BNE   ud1   
E48A   60           UD9:      RTS      
E48B                             ; =============================================================================
E48B                             ;  Console
E48B                             ; =============================================================================
E48B                             ; tosget: A = the byte at TOS, and TOS moves on.  inctos: TOS moves on.
E48B   A0 00        TOSGET:   LDY   #0   
E48D   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E48F   E6 02        INCTOS:   INC   TL   
E491   D0 02                  BNE   tg1   
E493   E6 03                  INC   TH   
E495   60           TG1:      RTS      
E496                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
E496                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
E496                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
E496                             ; The checked build walks a copy of TOS along the string, so that the address
E496                             ; is still there if it stops with Q on a NUL.
E496                H_PRINT:      
E496                          IF   CHECKED   
E496   20 76 E1               JSR   push   ; the copy
E499   20 9E E4               JSR   pr0   
E49C   D0 24                  BNE   pdrop   ; always (drop leaves Z clear): the address
E49E                PR0:         
E49E                          ENDIF      
E49E   20 8B E4               JSR   tosget   
E4A1   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E4A3   F0 1D                  BEQ   pdrop   
E4A5                          IF   CHECKED   
E4A5   A8                     TAY      ; (Y is free here)
E4A6   F0 0F                  BEQ   e_qpr   
E4A8                          ENDIF      
E4A8   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E4AA   D0 05                  BNE   pr1   
E4AC   20 8B E4               JSR   tosget   
E4AF   29 BF                  AND   #0BFh   
E4B1   20 03 FF     PR1:      JSR   CONOUT   
E4B4                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JMP   h_print   
E4B4                          ENDIF      
E4B4                          IF   CHECKED   
E4B4   4C 9E E4               JMP   pr0   
E4B7   20 F1 E2     E_QPR:    JSR   drop   ; the copy goes: the address is TOS again
E4BA   4C 0C E2               JMP   e_quote   ; $ ran into the end
E4BD                          ENDIF      
E4BD   A5 02        H_EMIT:   LDA   TL   ; "'"
E4BF   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E4C2   4C F1 E2     PDROP:    JMP   drop   
E4C5                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it. The
E4C5                             ; digits are divided off and held on the hardware stack, ended by a 0. udiv
E4C5                             ; leaves each remainder in the NOS cell, so a spare cell is opened for it.
E4C5   A5 03        H_NUM:    LDA   TH   
E4C7   10 08                  BPL   pn1   
E4C9   A9 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
E4CB   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E4CE   20 4D E3               JSR   neg   
E4D1   CA           PN1:      DEX      ; the spare cell
E4D2   A9 0A                  LDA   #10   
E4D4   85 08                  STA   D0   
E4D6   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E4D8   85 09                  STA   D1   
E4DA   48                     PHA      ; the end marker
E4DB   20 4A E4     PN2:      JSR   udiv   
E4DE   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E4E1   09 30                  ORA   #"0"   
E4E3   48                     PHA      
E4E4   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E4E6   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E4E8   D0 F1                  BNE   pn2   
E4EA   E8                     INX      
E4EB   68           PN3:      PLA      
E4EC   F0 D4                  BEQ   pdrop   
E4EE   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E4F1   4C EB E4               JMP   pn3   
E4F4   A0 01        H_FETCH:   LDY   #1   ; "@"
E4F6   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E4F8   48                     PHA      ; the high byte, while "," gets the low one
E4F9   20 00 E5               JSR   h_cfetch   
E4FC   68                     PLA      
E4FD   85 03                  STA   TH   
E4FF   60                     RTS      
E500                H_CFETCH:      ; ","
E500   A0 00                  LDY   #0   
E502   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E504   85 02        CF2:      STA   TL   ; TOS = A (Y = 0)
E506   84 03                  STY   TH   
E508   60                     RTS      
E509                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
E509                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
E509                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
E509                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
E509                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
E509   A5 03        H_KEY:    LDA   TH   
E50B   30 28                  BMI   line   
E50D   A0 28        KT1:      LDY   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
E50F   20 BA E0     KT2:      JSR   getk   
E512   D0 1D                  BNE   kt3   
E514   88                     DEY      
E515   D0 F8                  BNE   kt2   
E517   EE 76 04               INC   SEED   ; a millisecond with no key stirs the random
E51A   D0 03                  BNE   kt5   ;   seed by one: how long a key takes to come
E51C   EE 77 04               INC   SEED+1   ;   is the one thing here that is not the
E51F                KT5:         ;   same every time
E51F   A5 02                  LDA   TL   ; count the millisecond off:
E521   D0 06                  BNE   kt4   
E523   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E525   F0 E6                  BEQ   kt1   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
E527   C6 03                  DEC   TH   
E529   C6 02        KT4:      DEC   TL   
E52B   D0 E0                  BNE   kt1   
E52D   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E52F   D0 DC                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
E531   A0 00        KT3:      LDY   #0   
E533   F0 CF                  BEQ   cf2   ; always: TOS = A
E535                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
E535                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
E535                             ; is full. Y = the length so far; TL = the most allowed.
E535   20 4D E3     LINE:     JSR   neg   ; TOS = the count, and A = its high byte
E538   D0 04                  BNE   ln0   
E53A   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E53C   10 04                  BPL   ln1   
E53E   A9 7F        LN0:      LDA   #127   ; more than 127 is taken as 127
E540   85 02                  STA   TL   
E542   A0 00        LN1:      LDY   #0   
E544   F0 03                  BEQ   ln2   ; always
E546   20 03 FF     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
E549   20 BA E0     LN2:      JSR   getk   
E54C   F0 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
E54E   C9 0D                  CMP   #13   
E550   F0 14                  BEQ   ln5   
E552   C9 08                  CMP   #8   
E554   F0 0A                  BEQ   ln4   
E556   C4 02                  CPY   TL   
E558   B0 EF                  BCS   ln2   ; full
E55A   99 80 04               STA   LINEBUF,Y   
E55D   C8                     INY      
E55E   D0 E6                  BNE   ln3   ; always: echo it
E560   88           LN4:      DEY      ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
E561   10 E3                  BPL   ln3   
E563   C8                     INY      ;   unless the line was empty
E564   F0 E3                  BEQ   ln2   ; always
E566   99 80 04     LN5:      STA   LINEBUF,Y   ; A = CR
E569   A9 80                  LDA   #<LINEBUF   
E56B   85 02                  STA   TL   
E56D   A9 04                  LDA   #>LINEBUF   
E56F   85 03                  STA   TH   
E571   60                     RTS      
E572                             ; =============================================================================
E572                             ;  The grave
E572                             ; =============================================================================
E572                             ; The grave is a prefix: with the character after it, it is one command.
E572                             ; GCH holds the characters and GLO, beside it, the low byte of each one's
E572                             ; handler (less 1, for the RTS trick). The high byte is worked out: the
E572                             ; handlers lie in the order of the table and take up less than a page, so
E572                             ; they start in one page or in two, and GK is the place in the table where
E572                             ; the second page begins (the assembler works it out, and chktab6502.py
E572                             ; checks it). A handler starts with Y = its place in the table, and ends in
E572                             ; RTS. A character that is not in the table is unsafe: the unchecked build
E572                             ; does nothing, the checked build stops with W.
E572                             ; 
E572                             ;    `!  ( addr -- )        call the machine code at addr: see the contract
E572                             ;                           in the header
E572                             ;    `$  ( addr -- addr' )  the hex loader: pairs of hex digits are stored
E572                             ;                           from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS
E572                             ;                           (60h) is written and its address is left. An odd
E572                             ;                           last digit is consumed and dropped.
E572                             ;    `'  ( -- )             new line: CR LF
E572                             ;    `+  ( addr -- n )      add 1 to the cell at addr and leave its new value
E572                             ;    `,  ( n -- r )         a random number from 0 to n-1 (n is 1 to 32767)
E572                             ;    `-  ( addr -- n )      subtract 1 from the cell at addr, the same way
E572                             ;    `.  ( -- addr )        the address of the random seed
E572                             ;    `<  ( a b -- n )       the smaller of the two (signed)
E572                             ;    `>  ( a b -- n )       the larger
E572                             ;    `?  ( flag -- )        the cursor off (0) or on
E572                             ;    `@  ( row col -- )     the cursor to that row and column, both from 0
E572                             ;    `^  ( -- )             clear the screen and home the cursor
E572                             ;    `_  ( -- )             clear from the cursor to the end of the line
E572                H_GRAVE:      
E572                          IF   CHECKED   
E572   E6 06                  INC   PLACE   ; the place of anything that goes wrong in
E574   D0 02                  BNE   gr0   ;   one of these is the character after the
E576   E6 07                  INC   PLACE+1   ;   grave
E578                GR0:         
E578                          ENDIF      
E578   20 BC E2               JSR   getc   
E57B   A0 0C                  LDY   #GLO-GCH-1   
E57D   D9 94 E5     GR1:      CMP   GCH,Y   
E580   F0 06                  BEQ   gr2   
E582   88                     DEY      
E583   10 F8                  BPL   gr1   
E585                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RTS      ; no such code
E585                          ENDIF      
E585                          IF   CHECKED   
E585   4C A8 E1               JMP   eb1   ; no such code: W
E588                          ENDIF      
E588   C0 06        GR2:      CPY   #GK   ; carry: the second page
E58A   A9 E5                  LDA   #GQ0   
E58C   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E58E   48                     PHA      
E58F   B9 A1 E5               LDA   GLO,Y   
E592   48                     PHA      
E593   60                     RTS      ; to the handler
E594                             ; (The order matters: "-" just before "+", "<" at an odd place and ">" at
E594                             ; the even one after it, and the handlers in the same order in memory.)
E594   24 21 27     GCH:      DB   "$","!",27h   
E597   2D 2B 2E 2C 3C 3E 3F 40 5E 5F GMINUS:   DB   "-","+",".",",","<",">","?","@","^","_"   
E5A1   AD           GLO:      DB   (g_hex-1) & 0FFh   
E5A2   CB                     DB   (exec-1) & 0FFh   
E5A3   D9                     DB   (g_nl-1) & 0FFh   
E5A4   E3                     DB   (g_inc-1) & 0FFh   
E5A5   E3                     DB   (g_inc-1) & 0FFh   
E5A6   FE                     DB   (g_seed-1) & 0FFh   
E5A7   05                     DB   (g_rnd-1) & 0FFh   
E5A8   44                     DB   (g_min-1) & 0FFh   
E5A9   44                     DB   (g_min-1) & 0FFh   
E5AA   52                     DB   (g_cur-1) & 0FFh   
E5AB   6F                     DB   (g_at-1) & 0FFh   
E5AC   95                     DB   (g_cls-1) & 0FFh   
E5AD   9D                     DB   (g_eol-1) & 0FFh   
E5AE                             ; The page of each handler, and GK: 13 less the table entries whose handler
E5AE                             ; is in the second page. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down
E5AE                             ; when it stores a value.)
E5AE                GQ0:      EQU   (g_hex-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ1:      EQU   (exec-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ2:      EQU   (g_nl-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ3:      EQU   (g_inc-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ5:      EQU   (g_seed-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ6:      EQU   (g_rnd-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ7:      EQU   (g_min-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ9:      EQU   (g_cur-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ10:     EQU   (g_at-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ11:     EQU   (g_cls-1)/256   
E5AE                GQ12:     EQU   (g_eol-1)/256   
E5AE                GK:       EQU   13+12*GQ0-GQ1-GQ2-GQ3-GQ3-GQ5-GQ6-GQ7-GQ7-GQ9-GQ10-GQ11-GQ12   
E5AE                             ; `$ (never checked: the spec says so)
E5AE   20 A5 E2     G_HEX:    JSR   rdhex   
E5B1   B0 14                  BCS   hx2   
E5B3   0A                     ASL      
E5B4   0A                     ASL      
E5B5   0A                     ASL      
E5B6   0A                     ASL      
E5B7   85 04                  STA   T0   
E5B9   20 A5 E2               JSR   rdhex   
E5BC   B0 09                  BCS   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
E5BE   05 04                  ORA   T0   
E5C0   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   ; Y is 0 after rdhex
E5C2   20 8F E4               JSR   inctos   
E5C5   90 E7                  BCC   g_hex   ; always (rdhex left the carry clear)
E5C7   A9 60        HX2:      LDA   #60h   
E5C9   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E5CB   60                     RTS      
E5CC                             ; `!
E5CC   A5 02        EXEC:     LDA   TL   
E5CE   85 04                  STA   T0   
E5D0   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E5D2   85 05                  STA   T1   
E5D4   20 F1 E2               JSR   drop   ; the address is consumed
E5D7   6C 04 00               JMP   (T0)   
E5DA   A9 0D        G_NL:     LDA   #13   
E5DC   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E5DF   A9 0A                  LDA   #10   
E5E1   4C 03 FF               JMP   CONOUT   
E5E4                             ; `+ and `-: one routine. It adds 0000h with the carry set, or FFFFh with it
E5E4                             ; clear: SBC turns the carry into that 00 or FF and leaves the carry as it
E5E4                             ; was. Then "@" fetches the new value.
E5E4                G_INC:       
E5E4                          IF   CHECKED   
E5E4   20 34 E4               JSR   chk2   ; both bytes must be in the program's space
E5E7                          ENDIF      
E5E7   C0 04                  CPY   #GMINUS-GCH+1   ; carry: "+"
E5E9   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E5EB   E9 00                  SBC   #0   
E5ED   85 05                  STA   T1   
E5EF   A0 00                  LDY   #0   
E5F1   71 02                  ADC   (TL),Y   
E5F3   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E5F5   C8                     INY      
E5F6   A5 05                  LDA   T1   
E5F8   71 02                  ADC   (TL),Y   
E5FA   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E5FC   4C F4 E4               JMP   h_fetch   
E5FF                             ; `. pushes the address of the random seed.
E5FF   A9 76        G_SEED:   LDA   #<SEED   
E601   A0 04                  LDY   #>SEED   
E603   4C 6C E1               JMP   pushay   
E606                             ; `, ( n -- r ). The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes
E606                             ; every 16-bit value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones
E606                             ; and the low ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low
E606                             ; (EOR) before the remainder of dividing by n is taken.
E606                             ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
E606                             ; than 1.
E606                G_RND:       
E606                          IF   CHECKED   
E606   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E608   30 04                  BMI   gr9   
E60A   05 02                  ORA   TL   
E60C   D0 03                  BNE   gr8   
E60E   4C 29 E4     GR9:      JMP   e_zero   
E611                GR8:         
E611                          ENDIF      
E611   AD 76 04               LDA   SEED   
E614   AC 77 04               LDY   SEED+1   
E617   20 6C E1               JSR   pushay   ; the seed,
E61A   A9 05                  LDA   #05h   ;   and 261 (0105h) on top of it
E61C   A0 01                  LDY   #01h   
E61E   20 6C E1               JSR   pushay   
E621   20 84 E3               JSR   h_mul   ; TOS = seed * 261, and n is under it again
E624   20 8F E4               JSR   inctos   
E627   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E629   8D 76 04               STA   SEED   
E62C   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E62E   8D 77 04               STA   SEED+1   
E631   45 02                  EOR   TL   
E633   85 02                  STA   TL   
E635   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E638   85 08                  STA   D0   
E63A   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E63D   85 09                  STA   D1   ; D = n
E63F   20 4A E4               JSR   udiv   ; the remainder goes where n was,
E642   4C F1 E2               JMP   drop   ;   and comes up as TOS
E645                             ; `< and `>: one routine. scmp leaves the carry clear if a < b. Y is odd for
E645                             ; "<" and even for ">" (their places in the table), so the low bit of Y plus
E645                             ; the carry is set when a, the cell below, is the one to keep.
E645   20 64 E3     G_MIN:    JSR   scmp   
E648   98                     TYA      
E649   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E64B   4A                     LSR      
E64C   90 03                  BCC   gm1   
E64E   4C F1 E2               JMP   drop   ; a
E651   E8           GM1:      INX      ; b
E652   60                     RTS      
E653                          IF   ANSI   
E653                             ; `? ( flag -- ): ESC [ ? 2 5 l hides the cursor, ESC [ ? 2 5 h shows it.
E653   A0 04        G_CUR:    LDY   #4   
E655   B9 6B E6     GC1:      LDA   GQ25,Y   
E658   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E65B   88                     DEY      
E65C   10 F7                  BPL   gc1   
E65E   20 D1 E2               JSR   flag   
E661   F0 03                  BEQ   gc2   
E663   A9 68                  LDA   #"h"   
E665   2C                     DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
E666   A9 6C        GC2:      LDA   #"l"   
E668   4C 03 FF               JMP   CONOUT   
E66B   35 32 3F 5B 1B GQ25:   DB   "5","2","?","[",27   ; (printed from the end)
E670                             ; `@ ( row col -- ): ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H. (ANSI counts from 1.)
E670   20 8C E6     G_AT:     JSR   csi   
E673   20 AC E3               JSR   h_swap   ; the row on top
E676   20 86 E6               JSR   pinc   
E679   A9 3B                  LDA   #";"   
E67B   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E67E   20 86 E6               JSR   pinc   
E681   A9 48                  LDA   #"H"   
E683   4C 03 FF               JMP   CONOUT   
E686                             ; pinc: print TOS + 1, unsigned, and drop it
E686   20 8F E4     PINC:     JSR   inctos   
E689   4C D1 E4               JMP   pn1   
E68C                             ; csi: print ESC [, which starts every ANSI sequence. Keeps X and Y.
E68C   A9 1B        CSI:      LDA   #27   
E68E   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E691   A9 5B                  LDA   #"["   
E693   4C 03 FF               JMP   CONOUT   
E696                             ; `^: ESC [ H homes the cursor, and ESC [ J clears from there to the end of
E696                             ; the screen. `_: ESC [ K clears to the end of the line.
E696   A0 48        G_CLS:    LDY   #"H"   
E698   20 A0 E6               JSR   csiy   
E69B   A0 4A                  LDY   #"J"   
E69D   2C                     DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
E69E   A0 4B        G_EOL:    LDY   #"K"   
E6A0                             ; csiy: print ESC [ and the character in Y
E6A0   20 8C E6     CSIY:     JSR   csi   
E6A3   98                     TYA      
E6A4   4C 03 FF               JMP   CONOUT   
E6A7                          ENDIF      
E6A7                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's own routines do the work (see the equates).
                    G_CUR:    JSR   flag   ; A = 0 and Z set: off
                              JMP   CONCUR   
                    G_AT:     LDY   DSL,X   ; Y = the row
                              LDA   TL   ; A = the column
                              JSR   CONAT   
                              INX      
                              JMP   drop   
                    G_CLS:    JMP   CONCLS   
                    G_EOL:    JMP   CONEOL   
E6A7                          ENDIF      
E6A7                          IF   CHECKED   
E6A7                             ; =============================================================================
E6A7                             ;  Checked build: the error report
E6A7                             ; =============================================================================
E6A7                             ; error: the report, then EXIT. A = the letter, PLACE = the place, X = the
E6A7                             ; data stack to show, RSV = S for the Rtn line. Nothing here relies on S: an
E6A7                             ; overflowed or underflowed hardware stack wraps inside its page, and only
E6A7                             ; its depth is shown.
E6A7                             ;   CR LF
E6A7                             ;   Err X @ line,col CR LF
E6A7                             ;   Stk n: [...] and the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top  CR LF
E6A7                             ;   Rtn n CR LF
E6A7                             ; The numbers go through "#" (prnum), which pushes them over the data stack
E6A7                             ; and pops them again, so the stack is shown as it was.
E6A7   48           ERROR:    PHA      ; the letter
E6A8   A0 00                  LDY   #M_ERR-MSG   
E6AA   20 29 E7               JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Err "
E6AD   68                     PLA      
E6AE   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E6B1   20 29 E7               JSR   prs   ; " @ " (it follows M_ERR)
E6B4   20 54 E7               JSR   lcol   
E6B7   A5 08                  LDA   D0   
E6B9   A4 09                  LDY   D1   
E6BB   20 23 E7               JSR   prnum   ; the line
E6BE   A9 2C                  LDA   #","   
E6C0   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E6C3   A5 0A                  LDA   CL   
E6C5   A4 0B                  LDY   CL+1   
E6C7   20 23 E7               JSR   prnum   ; the column
E6CA   A0 0B                  LDY   #M_STK-MSG   
E6CC   20 29 E7               JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Stk "
E6CF   8A                     TXA      
E6D0   49 FF                  EOR   #0FFh   
E6D2   38                     SEC      
E6D3   E9 03                  SBC   #0FFh-DSE   ; the depth, DSE - X (FFh, an overflow: 253)
E6D5   48                     PHA      
E6D6   20 21 E7               JSR   prnum8   
E6D9   68                     PLA      
E6DA   A0 16                  LDY   #M_C-MSG   ; ":"
E6DC   C9 09                  CMP   #9   
E6DE   90 04                  BCC   er3   
E6E0   A9 08                  LDA   #8   ; more than 8: ": ..." and the top 8
E6E2   A0 11                  LDY   #M_CD-MSG   
E6E4   85 05        ER3:      STA   T1   ; T1 = how many cells to show
E6E6   20 29 E7               JSR   prs   
E6E9   20 76 E1               JSR   push   ; TOS into memory with the rest: cell i from
E6EC                             ;   the top is at DSL+X+i now
E6EC   A5 05        ER4:      LDA   T1   ; cells T1-1 down to 0, the top last
E6EE   F0 1B                  BEQ   er5   
E6F0   C6 05                  DEC   T1   
E6F2   A9 20                  LDA   #" "   
E6F4   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E6F7   8A                     TXA      
E6F8   18                     CLC      
E6F9   65 05                  ADC   T1   
E6FB   A8                     TAY      
E6FC   B9 00 02               LDA   DSL,Y   
E6FF   48                     PHA      
E700   B9 00 03               LDA   DSH,Y   
E703   A8                     TAY      
E704   68                     PLA      
E705   20 23 E7               JSR   prnum   
E708   4C EC E6               JMP   er4   
E70B   A0 17        ER5:      LDY   #M_RTN-MSG   
E70D   20 29 E7               JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Rtn "
E710   AD 35 04               LDA   RSV   
E713   49 FF                  EOR   #0FFh   
E715   4A                     LSR      ; (FFh - S) / 2 entries
E716   20 21 E7               JSR   prnum8   
E719   A0 09                  LDY   #M_NL-MSG   
E71B   20 29 E7               JSR   prs   
E71E   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   
E721                             ; prnum: print the number A (low), Y (high), signed, keeping the data stack.
E721                             ; prnum8: the same for A alone, 0-255.
E721   A0 00        PRNUM8:   LDY   #0   
E723   20 6C E1     PRNUM:    JSR   pushay   
E726   4C C5 E4               JMP   h_num   
E729                             ; prs: print the message at MSG+Y; its last byte has bit 7 set. Y ends just
E729                             ; past it, at the next message.
E729   B9 37 E7     PRS:      LDA   MSG,Y   
E72C   48                     PHA      
E72D   29 7F                  AND   #7Fh   
E72F   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E732   C8                     INY      
E733   68                     PLA      
E734   10 F3                  BPL   prs   
E736   60                     RTS      
E737                MSG:         
E737   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0 M_ERR:   DB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
E73D   20 40 A0               DB   " @"," "+80h   
E740   0D 8A        M_NL:     DB   13,10+80h   
E742   0D 0A 53 74 6B A0 M_STK:   DB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
E748   3A 20 2E 2E AE M_CD:   DB   ": ..","."+80h   
E74D   BA           M_C:      DB   ":"+80h   
E74E   0D 0A 52 74 6E A0 M_RTN:   DB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
E754                             ; lcol: the line (D0/D1) and the column (CL) of the place, both from 1. A
E754                             ; place below the program is in the -n? line buffer: line 0, and the column
E754                             ; is the place in the buffer. Otherwise IP (free now: the program has
E754                             ; stopped) runs from PROG to the place, counting LFs; CL keeps where the
E754                             ; last line started, and the column is the place minus that, plus 1.
E754   A9 00        LCOL:     LDA   #0   
E756   85 09                  STA   D1   
E758   85 08                  STA   D0   
E75A   A9 80                  LDA   #<LINEBUF   
E75C   85 0A                  STA   CL   
E75E   A9 04                  LDA   #>LINEBUF   
E760   85 0B                  STA   CL+1   
E762   A5 06                  LDA   PLACE   
E764   C9 00                  CMP   #<PROG   
E766   A5 07                  LDA   PLACE+1   
E768   E9 05                  SBC   #>PROG   
E76A   90 26                  BCC   lc9   ; below the program: line 0
E76C   E6 08                  INC   D0   
E76E   20 C8 E2               JSR   rstip   
E771   A5 00        LC3:      LDA   IP   ; a line starts here
E773   85 0A                  STA   CL   
E775   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E777   85 0B                  STA   CL+1   
E779   A5 00        LC1:      LDA   IP   
E77B   C5 06                  CMP   PLACE   
E77D   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E77F   E5 07                  SBC   PLACE+1   
E781   B0 0F                  BCS   lc9   ; at the place
E783   20 BC E2               JSR   getc   
E786   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E788   D0 EF                  BNE   lc1   
E78A   E6 08                  INC   D0   ; an LF: a new line starts after it
E78C   D0 E3                  BNE   lc3   
E78E   E6 09                  INC   D1   
E790   D0 DF                  BNE   lc3   ; always
E792   A5 06        LC9:      LDA   PLACE   
E794   38                     SEC      
E795   E5 0A                  SBC   CL   
E797   85 0A                  STA   CL   
E799   A5 07                  LDA   PLACE+1   
E79B   E5 0B                  SBC   CL+1   
E79D   85 0B                  STA   CL+1   
E79F   E6 0A                  INC   CL   ; + 1
E7A1   D0 02                  BNE   lc8   
E7A3   E6 0B                  INC   CL+1   
E7A5   60           LC8:      RTS      
E7A6                          ENDIF      


